NNAAMMEE
       basenc - Encode/decode data and print to standard output

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       bbaasseenncc [_O_P_T_I_O_N]... [_F_I_L_E]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       basenc encode or decode FILE, or standard input, to standard output.

       With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

       Mandatory  arguments  to  long  options are mandatory for short options
       too.

       ----bbaassee6644
              same as 'base64' program (RFC4648 section 4)

       ----bbaassee6644uurrll
              file- and url-safe base64 (RFC4648 section 5)

       ----bbaassee3322
              same as 'base32' program (RFC4648 section 6)

       ----bbaassee3322hheexx
              extended hex alphabet base32 (RFC4648 section 7)

       ----bbaassee1166
              hex encoding (RFC4648 section 8)

       ----bbaassee22mmssbbff
              bit string with most significant bit (msb) first

       ----bbaassee22llssbbff
              bit string with least significant bit (lsb) first

       --dd, ----ddeeccooddee
              decode data

       --ii, ----iiggnnoorree--ggaarrbbaaggee
              when decoding, ignore non-alphabet characters

       --ww, ----wwrraapp=_C_O_L_S
              wrap encoded lines after COLS character (default 76).  Use 0  to
              disable line wrapping

       ----zz8855  ascii85-like encoding (ZeroMQ spec:32/Z85); when encoding, input
              length must be a multiple of 4; when decoding, input length must
              be a multiple of 5

       ----hheellpp display this help and exit

       ----vveerrssiioonn
              output version information and exit

       When  decoding, the input may contain newlines in addition to the bytes
       of the formal alphabet.  Use ----iiggnnoorree--ggaarrbbaaggee  to  attempt  to  recover
       from any other non-alphabet bytes in the encoded stream.

EENNCCOODDIINNGGSS EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
              $ printf '\376\117\202' | basenc --base64
              /k+C

              $ printf '\376\117\202' | basenc --base64url
              _k-C

              $ printf '\376\117\202' | basenc --base32
              7ZHYE===

              $ printf '\376\117\202' | basenc --base32hex
              VP7O4===

              $ printf '\376\117\202' | basenc --base16
              FE4F82

              $ printf '\376\117\202' | basenc --base2lsbf
              011111111111001001000001

              $ printf '\376\117\202' | basenc --base2msbf
              111111100100111110000010

              $ printf '\376\117\202\000' | basenc --z85
              @.FaC

